Hyprland patch series for the side dock (features/sidedock), applied in order by
features/hyprland/nixos.nix under my.hyprland.keystone. Split 2026-10-08 from the
single trapezoid.patch; applying 01..11 onto the same base gives byte-for-byte the
tree trapezoid.patch did. 11 has since changed: it gained the 1:1 touch workspace swipe,
and on 2026-10-08 its hardcoded touch recognizers became a touch stream for Lua
(features/hyprland/touch.lua), touch claiming and hl.touch_swipe, then gained layer
awareness (touch/pen events' `layer`, hl.layer_at). 04 gained the far-toward-the-edge
dock dismiss (gestures:dock_swipe_dismiss) on 2026-10-09; the same day 03 mapped the pen
and touch motion through the keystone on every card, and touch-down on X11 cards. Each
patch's own header says what it does and why.

Base: Hyprland 0.56.2 + nixpkgs' monitor-soft-apply-logical-size.patch + the other
patches listed before this series in nixos.nix (layoutmanager-guard-null-space,
gamma-refused-control-zombie, input-on-monitor-loss,
soft-apply-mark-blur-dirty).

Bisectability: every prefix was checked for references to identifiers a later patch
introduces (none), but only the full series has been compiled. Known behavioural
gap in a prefix: before 10, a mouse press on a dock card's border tests the flat
box (03 makes only the hover cursor keystone-aware). Code comments inside the
patched sources still say "trapezoid.patch" where they predate the split; the
patches themselves must reproduce that source exactly.

Maintaining: keep the patches applying in order. To change one, apply the series
up to it on the base, edit, and regenerate it as the diff between consecutive
trees, so later patches still apply without fuzz.
